source: crates/hydronode-cli/tests/c3_help.rs
expression: text
---
Sign in to HydroNode. Without a flag you choose how.

--web opens the browser and signs you in like the web app.
--device shows a code to confirm on another device (SSH, no browser).
--token / --with-token use an API token: hat_ reads and writes, hrt_ only reads.

Usage: hn login [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --web         Sign in with the browser (recommended)
      --device      Show a code to confirm on another device
      --token       Paste an API token (hidden input)
      --with-token  Read an API token from stdin
      --no-browser  Do not open a browser, only print the link
  -h, --help        Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn login
  hn login --device
  echo "$HYDRONODE_TOKEN" | hn login --with-token
  hn -p work login --web
